#!/usr/bin/env python3
# Software: install apps from the package repositories and update the whole system.
# The catalog comes from AppStream (archlinux-appstream-data), the phone rating from
# display_length and /usr/share/plinius-software/apps.conf. Package operations are done by
# plinius-pkg via pkexec; this app is only the user interface for it (docs/PAKETIERUNG.md).
#
# Usage: plinius-software                  open the app
#        plinius-software --check-updates  check once and notify (plinius-software-check.timer)
#        plinius-software --updates-json   check once, print the result as JSON (Settings)
#
# Settings (gnome-control-center-plinius) has the same pages: Apps (Explore, Installed,
# Settings) and System/Security > Updates. Its Updates page asks --updates-json, so the check
# and the approval rules (plinius-freigabe) exist only here. The app itself is no longer in the
# app grid; the update notification opens Settings on the Updates page.
# SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT

